      0,
      'The Perceptual Quantizer, standardized as SMPTE ST 2084 in 2014 based on research by Dolby engineers, maps digital code values to absolute brightness levels according to a model of human contrast sensitivity across a much wider luminance range than traditional gamma curves used for standard-dynamic-range video, allowing HDR10 and Dolby Vision content to specify highlights far brighter than SDR\'s roughly 100-nit reference while still allocating enough code values to shadow detail. Hybrid Log-Gamma, developed jointly by the BBC and Japan\'s NHK, is a competing HDR transfer function designed to remain backward-compatible with SDR displays without needing separate metadata, making it more common in live broadcast HDR than in cinema or streaming HDR. Rec. 709 and S-Log3 are unrelated: Rec. 709 is the long-standing SDR broadcast gamma standard, and S-Log3 is Sony\'s proprietary log encoding curve for on-set capture, not a delivery HDR standard. Trivia: PQ\'s absolute-brightness design means the same code value always corresponds to the same nit level regardless of the display, unlike traditional relative gamma curves.',
